:: MMA Gym Avery First Response
<<effects>>
<<if $mmaGymAWChoice is "form">>
	Avery walks over and points at your shoulders. "You're holding them too high. You're wasting effort before the exercise even starts."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> points to an empty bench and shows you where to put your feet. "Try again, slower this time. Get the movement right before you worry about speed."
	<br><br>
	You copy the position. Avery watches the first repetition, then reaches over to adjust your grip before you start the second.<<gtiredness>><<gstress>><<stress 4>><<tiredness 10>>
	<br><br>
	"And stop looking so offended," <<he>> says. "I'm fixing your form, not insulting your family."<<npcincr Avery dom 1>><<gdom>><<pass 10>>
<<elseif $mmaGymAWChoice is "status">>
	You ask what Avery thinks of the gym.
	<br><br>
	Avery looks around the room before answering. "The equipment is acceptable. The ventilation is decent, but there's almost no privacy."
	<br><br>
	A few metres away, someone drops a loaded barbell onto the floor and grunts loudly.
	<br><br>
	Avery looks towards them, then back at you. "That is the problem. Good equipment doesn't help people who refuse to learn how to use it."<<pass 5>>
<<elseif $mmaGymAWChoice is "watch">>
	Avery notices you watching <<him>> in the mirror. Instead of leaving, <<he>> steps back onto the treadmill and raises the incline by two levels.
	"If you're going to stare, at least pay attention. You might learn something."
	<br><br>
	The treadmill speeds up. Avery keeps the same running form, but after several minutes <<his>> hands tighten around the rails and sweat darkens the back of <<his>> shirt.
	<br><br>
	"Cardio is simple," Avery says while continuing to run. "The difficult part is keeping your form when you're tired. That's when people start making excuses."<<pass 5>>
<<else>>
	"To train?" Avery repeats. <<He>> looks at you, then at the machines around the room.
	"Then train properly. Wandering between machines until you feel tired is not a plan."
	<br><br>
	Avery taps <<his>> treadmill display. The screen shows timed intervals, heart-rate targets, and rest periods.
	<br><br>
	"I decide what I'm doing before I start," <<he>> says. "It makes it harder to quit early and pretend I meant to."<<npcincr Avery love 1>><<stress -3>><<pass 10>><<glove>><<lstress>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|MMA Gym Avery First Offer]]>><</link>>

:: MMA Gym Avery First Offer
<<effects>>
Avery steps off the treadmill with efficiency. <<He>> folds <<his>> towel, checks <<his>> watch, and turns to you, looking like <<hes>> already bored.
"Your gear is a disaster. Your form is worse. I've seen better training in a daycare."
<br><br>
Before you can decide if <<hes>> insulting you or just stating a fact, <<he>> continues.
<br><br>
"There's a premium tier here. Private lockers, decent showers, and fewer people... I could get you access.
It would be significantly less painful than watching you improvise for another month."
<br><br>
It's phrased as a generous offer, but it lands like a direct command.
<br><br>
"But for now," <<he>> says, already walking toward the exit, "you're joining me for a smoothie in the lounge. It's organic,
absurdly expensive, and marginally tolerable if you order the right one."
<br><br>
Avery doesn't wait for your answer. <<Hes>> already headed for the lounge.
<br><br>
<<link [[Join Avery in the lounge (0:20)|MMA Gym Avery First End]]>><<set $mmaGymAWChoice2 to "accept">><<pass 20>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Say you don't need Avery's money (0:05)|MMA Gym Avery First End]]>><<set $mmaGymAWChoice2 to "refuse">><<pass 5>><</link>>

